import numpy as np

def join_on_eq_with_dt(a1, a2, t1, t2, dt, abs_rel):
    I = []
    J = []
    if abs_rel == "abs_dt":
        for i in range(len(a1)):
            for j in range(len(a2)):
                if a1[i] == a2[j] and abs(t1[i] - t2[j]) <= dt:
                    I.append(i)
                    J.append(j)
    elif abs_rel == "rel_dt":
        for i in range(len(a1)):
            for j in range(len(a2)):
                if a1[i] == a2[j] and abs(t1[i] - t2[j]) / max(abs(t1[i]), abs(t2[j])) <= dt:
                    I.append(i)
                    J.append(j)
    return np.array(I), np.array(J)
```

This solution defines the `join_on_eq_with_dt` function that iterates through the input arrays `a1` and `a2` and their corresponding time arrays `t1` and `t2`. Depending on the `abs_rel` parameter, it checks for equality with either absolute or relative time difference within the specified time window `dt`. The function then returns the indices of matching elements in arrays `I` and `J`. If no matches are found within the time window, empty arrays are returned.

