In the solution, the `SingletonMeta` metaclass is implemented to enforce the Singleton pattern. The `__call__` method checks if an instance of the class already exists and creates a new instance if it doesn't. The `MyClass` is defined using the `SingletonMeta` metaclass, ensuring that only one instance of `MyClass` is created. The testing code demonstrates that both `obj1` and `obj2` refer to the same instance, confirming the enforcement of the Singleton pattern.

